cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  PoliScreen: reproducible virtual screening with objective
  interaction-quality scoring
message: >-
  If you use PoliScreen in published work, please cite it as
  below. Cite also the tools it runs (AutoDock Vina, ADCP, PLIP,
  RDKit, Open Babel, fpocket and, where applicable, gnina and
  ADMET-AI); the full list with references is in the "How to
  cite" panel of the interface and in the Methods file the
  application exports.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anaya Guerrero
    given-names: Diego César
    email: diego.anayagro@gmail.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DiegoAnyG/PoliScreen'
abstract: >-
  A virtual-screening platform that closes the loop of design,
  synthesizability filtering, molecular docking, interaction-quality
  evaluation and ADMET prediction. Unlike screening panels that rank
  by affinity and contact count, PoliScreen scores binding quality by
  weighting each contact by bond type and residue role, normalizes
  against the fingerprint of the crystallographic ligand, and pairs
  every result with a confidence metric built from independent lines
  of evidence. It routes ligands to the engine suited to their nature
  (AutoDock Vina for small molecules, AutoDock CrankPep for peptides)
  and validates the setup by redocking the co-crystallized control.
keywords:
  - virtual screening
  - molecular docking
  - protein-ligand interactions
  - peptide docking
  - reproducibility
  - cheminformatics
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.1.0
